# Paper Reading Agent Workflow

## Discovery
The repository uses `reading_queue.md` as the human-facing tracker and
`data/paper_registry.json` as the permanent deduplication/state database.

Valid statuses are exactly:
- 🔴 To read
- 🟡 Review ready
- 🟢 Done

Never create another status label.

## Deep reading lifecycle
When the user asks to deep-read a paper that exists in `reading_queue.md`:

1. Identify the exact paper row and its stable registry record.
2. Leave/set its status to `🔴 To read` while preparing the reading task.
3. Use the existing `paper-deep-reading` skill to create/update the structured note under `notes/`.
4. Add the generated note link to the paper's `Notes` cell.
5. Change the paper status in BOTH:
   - `reading_queue.md`
   - `data/paper_registry.json`
   to `🟡 Review ready`.
6. Commit and push only the files touched by this reading task.

When the user says they have reviewed/finished/approved that paper:
1. Change status in BOTH tracker and registry to `🟢 Done`.
2. Preserve the note link.
3. Commit and push.

A `🟢 Done` paper remains in the tracker/history and must never be rediscovered as a new item.

## Weekly discovery
When the automated discovery script runs:
- previously registered papers are never duplicated;
- status and notes are preserved;
- only genuinely unseen papers start as `🔴 To read`;
- metadata/ranking may refresh without resetting workflow state.
